cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmarking framework in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "fmbenchmark: Benchmarking Framework for Statistical Fine-Mapping Methods"
authors:
  - family-names: "Siu"
    given-names: "Lucas"
    affiliation: "Imperial College London"
    email: "ls1020@ic.ac.uk"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucassiu14/fine-mapping-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/lucassiu14/fine-mapping-benchmark"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-03"
keywords:
  - fine-mapping
  - GWAS
  - benchmarking
  - statistical-genetics
  - simulation
  - susieR
  - PolyFun
abstract: >-
  An R framework for benchmarking statistical fine-mapping methods using
  simulated genetic data. Supports a catalogue of fine-mapping methods
  (SuSiE, SuSiE-inf, FINEMAP, FINEMAP-inf, CAVIAR, FiniMOM, ABF, CARMA,
  PAINTOR, Funmap, PolyFun, SBayesRC, SparsePro, BEATRICE and Functional
  BEATRICE, plus marginal-z and oracle-prior baselines) with simulated
  genotypes derived from 1000 Genomes Phase 3 haplotypes, flexible per-locus
  and genome-wide simulation pipelines, and evaluation via average precision,
  credible-set coverage, power and size, PIP calibration and runtime,
  reported per region so results can be summarised along any axis.
